1
00:00:13,888 --> 00:00:16,933
OUR STICKY LOVE

2
00:00:50,717 --> 00:00:51,593
Kaito!

3
00:01:03,897 --> 00:01:04,731
Fuck.

4
00:01:09,069 --> 00:01:10,070
What the…

5
00:01:24,793 --> 00:01:25,752
GUJIN RICE TAFFY

6
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:45,521
Honey! What are you doing here?

7
00:01:45,522 --> 00:01:48,315
Don't worry, honey. The ladies are here.

8
00:01:48,316 --> 00:01:49,483
So,

9
00:01:49,484 --> 00:01:53,153
all that turmoil that Tae-ha and Eun-sae
went through,

10
00:01:53,154 --> 00:01:55,405
and even Jeong-hwa's car accident…

11
00:01:55,406 --> 00:01:59,118
All along, that was all your doing?

12
00:01:59,119 --> 00:02:00,452
Hui-ja!

13
00:02:00,453 --> 00:02:03,872
- You don't seem to grasp the situation.
- Please don't.

14
00:02:03,873 --> 00:02:05,165
But these guys here--

15
00:02:05,166 --> 00:02:07,251
Hey, Geum-hyang!

16
00:02:07,252 --> 00:02:09,586
You ready?

17
00:02:09,587 --> 00:02:10,922
Aye.

18
00:02:12,423 --> 00:02:13,466
No problem.

19
00:02:15,802 --> 00:02:19,179
I was a shot put athlete
at Gujin Girls' Commercial High,

20
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:21,975
you sons of guns!

21
00:02:31,484 --> 00:02:35,738
How dare you bastards
come barging into our village!

22
00:02:36,531 --> 00:02:38,324
Come at me!

23
00:02:41,786 --> 00:02:43,871
Anyone who messes with us
Taffy Village folk

24
00:02:43,872 --> 00:02:46,291
better be saying their prayers.

25
00:03:03,099 --> 00:03:04,183
Hold up.

26
00:03:04,184 --> 00:03:07,603
Song-wol is from North Korea, right?

27
00:03:07,604 --> 00:03:08,563
Yeah.

28
00:03:09,147 --> 00:03:11,607
I did hear that she used to be a soldier.

29
00:03:11,608 --> 00:03:15,069
Who needs tear gas when you can mix
vinegar with red pepper powder?

30
00:03:19,532 --> 00:03:20,532
Damn it!

31
00:03:20,533 --> 00:03:24,494
- You! How dare you hit him!
- No, that way!

32
00:03:24,495 --> 00:03:26,581
I'll tear you limb from limb, you bastard!

33
00:03:27,332 --> 00:03:30,627
A son of a bitch like you
should have his guts ripped out

34
00:03:31,211 --> 00:03:34,671
and thrown into the mudflats,
but even the worms wouldn't eat you!

35
00:03:34,672 --> 00:03:38,592
How dare you touch my husband,
you absolute piece of filth!

36
00:03:38,593 --> 00:03:40,469
- Damn you! Die, you bastard!
- Stop her.

37
00:03:40,470 --> 00:03:41,720
- Honey.
- Stop her.

38
00:03:41,721 --> 00:03:44,390
Hey! He's my husband!

39
00:03:46,226 --> 00:03:49,144
Hang in there, okay? Just a little longer.

40
00:03:49,145 --> 00:03:50,437
Ma'am.

41
00:03:50,438 --> 00:03:52,272
- Hey, there you are.
- Yes.

42
00:03:52,273 --> 00:03:54,566
He's on our side,
but he's hurt pretty badly.

43
00:03:54,567 --> 00:03:56,652
You guys work at a hospital, so treat him.

44
00:03:56,653 --> 00:03:59,154
Are you… But ma'am,
we're a mental health clinic.

45
00:03:59,155 --> 00:04:00,197
Are you okay?

46
00:04:00,198 --> 00:04:01,783
- Yes, I'm okay.
- Where…

47
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:05,745
Watch out!

48
00:04:13,878 --> 00:04:16,589
- An Gi-jun, are you okay?
- Yeah, I'm okay.

49
00:04:17,382 --> 00:04:18,258
I'll be okay,

50
00:04:18,925 --> 00:04:20,301
as long as

51
00:04:21,177 --> 00:04:22,220
you're okay.

52
00:04:47,578 --> 00:04:48,788
Pil-seung?

53
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:57,087
- Why are you here?
- What?

54
00:04:57,088 --> 00:04:58,630
- What?
- It's dangerous!

55
00:04:58,631 --> 00:05:02,593
Why? What will I do with you?

56
00:05:13,229 --> 00:05:14,772
It's Eun-sae!

57
00:05:15,982 --> 00:05:17,816
Gang-rok, are you okay?

58
00:05:17,817 --> 00:05:18,651
Yes.

59
00:05:22,071 --> 00:05:23,406
What about Jang Tae-ha?

60
00:05:37,045 --> 00:05:37,879
Baek Sang-gil.

61
00:05:41,007 --> 00:05:42,717
I'll take whatever you give me.

62
00:05:45,136 --> 00:05:46,179
Just do it outside.

63
00:05:53,061 --> 00:05:55,480
Thought I wouldn't hear
the difference in your gloves?

64
00:05:56,981 --> 00:06:00,525
You think you can become
a national athlete with such dirty fists?

65
00:06:00,526 --> 00:06:03,071
Wouldn't it be good for you
if I make the national team?

66
00:06:05,156 --> 00:06:08,200
Taking you in as my disciple,
even for a short time,

67
00:06:08,201 --> 00:06:10,494
will have been
the most shameful thing in my life.

68
00:06:10,495 --> 00:06:13,247
- Coach!
- From this moment on, I'm not your coach.

69
00:06:14,082 --> 00:06:16,417
I never taught you
to use your fists to harm others.

70
00:06:21,839 --> 00:06:23,174
Fuck this!

71
00:06:41,567 --> 00:06:43,985
Plaster in your gloves? Are you crazy?

72
00:06:43,986 --> 00:06:45,196
Why would you do that?

73
00:06:46,114 --> 00:06:48,949
- I needed to win to get paid.
- What?

74
00:06:48,950 --> 00:06:52,870
They said they bet big on me winning
and that it would all be mine if I won.

75
00:06:54,288 --> 00:06:58,208
How will we ever afford an oil boiler
or buy a Grandeur on an athlete's stipend?

76
00:06:58,209 --> 00:06:59,794
Who asked you for any of that?

77
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:03,380
I liked boxing
because everyone was equal in the ring,

78
00:07:03,381 --> 00:07:06,591
fighting with nothing but their fists
regardless of status or wealth.

79
00:07:06,592 --> 00:07:10,805
And I liked you because of how you made it
this far with nothing but your fists.

80
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:19,313
So go back to your coach and beg, okay?

81
00:07:21,149 --> 00:07:22,233
Forget it.

82
00:07:22,817 --> 00:07:24,276
I can just quit boxing.

83
00:07:24,277 --> 00:07:25,361
Baek Sang-gil.

84
00:07:26,487 --> 00:07:28,322
Are you going to keep disappointing me?

85
00:07:29,282 --> 00:07:31,409
Then you can just leave me too!

86
00:07:34,745 --> 00:07:35,913
What did you say?

87
00:07:36,956 --> 00:07:39,584
I won't spend my life always losing
like the rest of you.

88
00:07:59,061 --> 00:07:59,896
Hi.

89
00:08:02,773 --> 00:08:06,234
Since you lost the match today,
I can't give you the money.

90
00:08:06,235 --> 00:08:08,738
But I was thinking I'd give you
something else instead.

91
00:08:09,238 --> 00:08:11,740
Once you're banned
from the boxing association,

92
00:08:11,741 --> 00:08:13,325
you won't be able to box anymore.

93
00:08:13,326 --> 00:08:15,912
Won't you need to find another way
to make a living?

94
00:09:11,217 --> 00:09:12,926
He'll be 100 days old next month.

95
00:09:12,927 --> 00:09:15,178
It's not too late
to get out and come back.

96
00:09:15,179 --> 00:09:17,390
A dad should be able to look his kid
in the eyes.

97
00:09:36,284 --> 00:09:37,118
Hey.

98
00:09:38,494 --> 00:09:39,620
Is it even my kid?

99
00:09:40,997 --> 00:09:43,123
- What?
- If you need money, find someone else.

100
00:09:43,124 --> 00:09:44,959
Don't drag random people into it.

101
00:10:19,952 --> 00:10:20,995
Why not just take it?

102
00:10:22,538 --> 00:10:25,166
Take this money, and in return,

103
00:10:25,833 --> 00:10:27,418
I never want to see you two again.

104
00:10:28,377 --> 00:10:29,587
Don't worry.

105
00:10:30,504 --> 00:10:31,589
This is the last time.

106
00:10:34,675 --> 00:10:38,887
I just thought I should show the baby
his father's face at least once.

107
00:10:38,888 --> 00:10:41,807
I thought that was my duty as his mother.

108
00:10:48,147 --> 00:10:50,274
You should say your last goodbye.

109
00:11:24,725 --> 00:11:27,060
Where's the money, you punk?
You don't have any?

110
00:11:27,061 --> 00:11:28,312
Then you should get beaten.

111
00:11:40,408 --> 00:11:42,201
Living honestly gets you nowhere.

112
00:11:43,285 --> 00:11:45,079
If you can't give your kid anything,

113
00:11:45,746 --> 00:11:48,040
then your kid will grow up always losing.

114
00:11:49,166 --> 00:11:53,713
I didn't want to live like that,
so I chose to win, whatever the means.

115
00:11:55,047 --> 00:11:55,965
So…

116
00:11:59,385 --> 00:12:00,386
just take the money.

117
00:12:02,221 --> 00:12:03,055
No.

118
00:12:05,474 --> 00:12:06,308
You lost.

119
00:12:08,394 --> 00:12:09,729
There's something in this world

120
00:12:11,063 --> 00:12:12,940
that you can never win against.

121
00:12:15,443 --> 00:12:17,026
Even if I have to starve,

122
00:12:17,027 --> 00:12:19,113
I won't raise my baby with dirty money.

123
00:12:20,197 --> 00:12:21,240
I won't

124
00:12:22,491 --> 00:12:23,701
raise my baby like that.

125
00:13:04,658 --> 00:13:06,535
<i>So I hope you'll prove it, sir.</i>

126
00:13:07,369 --> 00:13:08,996
That you're different from him.

127
00:13:11,207 --> 00:13:12,958
I'll get us some drinks.

128
00:13:24,136 --> 00:13:26,430
Why did you bring me to the funeral home?

129
00:13:28,724 --> 00:13:30,017
Thinking of your own father?

130
00:13:36,023 --> 00:13:37,024
I never met him.

131
00:13:38,484 --> 00:13:40,778
He passed away before I was born.

132
00:13:45,950 --> 00:13:48,577
Not having any memories might be better.

133
00:13:53,541 --> 00:13:54,917
I've never met him,

134
00:13:55,459 --> 00:13:57,086
but I heard he was a good man.

135
00:13:59,421 --> 00:14:00,673
If he were alive,

136
00:14:02,174 --> 00:14:04,718
I think I would have liked him a lot.

137
00:14:06,428 --> 00:14:08,806
Even if he wasn't a good man,

138
00:14:09,598 --> 00:14:11,308
I would still have liked to meet him.

139
00:14:14,728 --> 00:14:16,021
Because he's my father.

140
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:38,127
I don't know what you're trying to do,

141
00:14:38,627 --> 00:14:40,629
but don't make a scene
in front of Grandma.

142
00:14:41,463 --> 00:14:42,590
Let's take it outside.

143
00:14:44,925 --> 00:14:45,801
What a truly…

144
00:14:49,722 --> 00:14:51,348
cruel twist of fate,

145
00:14:52,349 --> 00:14:53,350
Jang Tae-ha.

146
00:15:15,706 --> 00:15:17,082
Baek Sang-gil!

147
00:15:41,357 --> 00:15:43,025
Don't run. Face the consequences.

148
00:16:00,876 --> 00:16:01,710
Consequences?

149
00:16:02,711 --> 00:16:04,837
It's a gift for taking off your gloves.

150
00:16:04,838 --> 00:16:07,633
From now on, get in fights
that reek of blood, not sweat.

151
00:16:09,385 --> 00:16:10,552
Tae-ha!

152
00:16:12,137 --> 00:16:15,641
<i>Every day, your imagination will
eat away at you, wondering…</i>

153
00:16:17,267 --> 00:16:19,186
<i>about my plan for you.</i>

154
00:16:32,282 --> 00:16:34,284
<i>No. You lost.</i>

155
00:16:35,577 --> 00:16:36,745
<i>I won't</i>

156
00:16:37,246 --> 00:16:38,664
raise my baby like that.

157
00:16:56,098 --> 00:16:57,474
Baek Sang-gil!

158
00:17:21,457 --> 00:17:22,583
No!

159
00:18:29,358 --> 00:18:30,609
Let's put…

160
00:18:34,738 --> 00:18:36,406
an end to this twisted fate of ours.

161
00:18:39,368 --> 00:18:40,202
No.

162
00:18:44,414 --> 00:18:46,333
No! You can't!

163
00:19:24,329 --> 00:19:29,501
You both always end a drinking session
with an order of gochujang stew.

164
00:19:36,675 --> 00:19:38,218
You like this too?

165
00:19:39,136 --> 00:19:39,970
Yes.

166
00:19:42,472 --> 00:19:44,266
You've got old-fashioned taste.

167
00:19:44,766 --> 00:19:46,018
It's good for hangovers.

168
00:21:10,894 --> 00:21:12,186
<i>You're going to do what?</i>

169
00:21:12,187 --> 00:21:15,731
A typhoon can carve out a path
where there was none.

170
00:21:15,732 --> 00:21:18,902
After our peaceful village
went through all that ruckus,

171
00:21:19,611 --> 00:21:23,447
I realized I can't just keep waiting
for my spiritual powers to return

172
00:21:23,448 --> 00:21:25,825
and that I should find a way
to make a living.

173
00:21:25,826 --> 00:21:26,910
So,

174
00:21:27,911 --> 00:21:29,453
you're learning tarot cards?

175
00:21:29,454 --> 00:21:33,834
These things are about as accurate
as a shaman's readings.

176
00:21:34,334 --> 00:21:37,295
All right, then. Give us a reading.

177
00:21:37,296 --> 00:21:40,173
Will there be another ruckus
in our village?

178
00:21:41,591 --> 00:21:43,509
Well, then. Shall I take a look?

179
00:21:43,510 --> 00:21:45,303
- Yeah.
- Okay.

180
00:21:45,304 --> 00:21:47,306
You have to shuffle these cards with care.

181
00:21:51,018 --> 00:21:52,311
All righty.

182
00:21:53,103 --> 00:21:54,020
Not bad.

183
00:21:54,021 --> 00:21:56,189
Let me see.

184
00:21:59,359 --> 00:22:00,944
I think it's this one.

185
00:22:09,536 --> 00:22:11,747
It says spring will come to many places.

186
00:22:18,962 --> 00:22:20,171
MUSCLE ACHES
BRUISES

187
00:22:20,172 --> 00:22:22,966
The bottom line is you got hurt saving me.

188
00:22:26,011 --> 00:22:27,387
Use this to treat it.

189
00:22:28,263 --> 00:22:29,264
I'll get going.

190
00:22:30,891 --> 00:22:32,893
I just couldn't figure it out.

191
00:22:34,853 --> 00:22:35,770
What?

192
00:22:35,771 --> 00:22:37,022
When I saw test papers,

193
00:22:38,315 --> 00:22:40,942
the answers would just pop into my head.

194
00:22:42,069 --> 00:22:45,155
But no matter how much
I looked into a woman's heart,

195
00:22:45,655 --> 00:22:46,740
I couldn't get it.

196
00:22:48,784 --> 00:22:53,538
You said you couldn't feel my sincerity,
but I had no idea what to do.

197
00:22:56,708 --> 00:22:58,627
To be honest, I still don't get it.

198
00:23:00,170 --> 00:23:03,590
If I were to just tell you
how I feel right now…

199
00:23:05,467 --> 00:23:07,219
I want to keep

200
00:23:08,470 --> 00:23:13,892
making memories with you,
like that time at the pub.

201
00:23:16,228 --> 00:23:17,562
Want some hangover soup?

202
00:23:25,695 --> 00:23:27,572
Go Eun-sae once said…

203
00:23:28,156 --> 00:23:30,282
Why get your memory back
if you believe him?

204
00:23:30,283 --> 00:23:31,992
How lonely must that be?

205
00:23:31,993 --> 00:23:35,831
Not being able to share the memories
you made with the person you love.

206
00:23:37,249 --> 00:23:39,626
Sharing the same memories

207
00:23:40,627 --> 00:23:43,755
means that you were
very close to each other.

208
00:23:45,048 --> 00:23:48,260
But since we were always bickering,
fighting over our pride,

209
00:23:48,844 --> 00:23:50,637
we couldn't share those moments.

210
00:23:52,139 --> 00:23:54,683
If I had amnesia too,

211
00:23:55,183 --> 00:23:57,686
I'd reset everything
and live my life anew.

212
00:23:58,979 --> 00:24:00,355
But I can't do that.

213
00:24:02,649 --> 00:24:03,525
So just…

214
00:24:08,989 --> 00:24:10,615
give me another chance.

215
00:24:18,790 --> 00:24:20,125
I know I look pathetic,

216
00:24:20,876 --> 00:24:24,838
saying we should break up
and then asking you to get back together.

217
00:24:26,965 --> 00:24:27,841
But

218
00:24:29,009 --> 00:24:30,760
I can't help still liking you.

219
00:24:42,522 --> 00:24:43,523
Hey.

220
00:24:44,107 --> 00:24:46,485
That's all you've got for your girlfriend?

221
00:24:49,070 --> 00:24:49,905
"Girlfriend"?

222
00:24:52,115 --> 00:24:54,493
Girlfriend… So are we…

223
00:24:55,076 --> 00:24:57,621
Then are we back…

224
00:25:14,554 --> 00:25:16,597
Come in for a second.

225
00:25:16,598 --> 00:25:18,974
What in the world is it
that you want to give me?

226
00:25:18,975 --> 00:25:19,851
Sit here.

227
00:25:20,936 --> 00:25:22,395
Are you giving me pocket money?

228
00:25:33,615 --> 00:25:34,532
These are…

229
00:25:34,533 --> 00:25:37,536
You used to love these. Do you remember?

230
00:25:43,959 --> 00:25:45,751
Let's see what our Tae-ha will pick.

231
00:25:45,752 --> 00:25:47,670
Let's grab one.

232
00:25:47,671 --> 00:25:49,129
Grab the gavel. Go on.

233
00:25:49,130 --> 00:25:50,757
Yes, that one. The doctor's…

234
00:25:52,133 --> 00:25:53,343
Come on.

235
00:25:55,428 --> 00:25:56,555
Dang it.

236
00:25:57,055 --> 00:25:59,348
Like mother, like son, I guess.

237
00:25:59,349 --> 00:26:01,392
A mom who's a boxing fan

238
00:26:01,393 --> 00:26:03,644
and puts boxing gloves
on the birthday table.

239
00:26:03,645 --> 00:26:06,064
And a son who grabs them right away.

240
00:26:06,565 --> 00:26:09,900
I guess Tae-ha will become a boxer
when he grows up.

241
00:26:09,901 --> 00:26:13,195
Picking gloves on his first birthday.
Maybe he'll make it to nationals.

242
00:26:13,196 --> 00:26:15,239
Well, aren't you Miss Glass-half-full.

243
00:26:15,240 --> 00:26:18,034
You see,
I believe in these sorts of things.

244
00:26:18,618 --> 00:26:20,579
That's why I named him "Tae-ha."

245
00:26:21,538 --> 00:26:24,290
No matter how much a big river meanders,

246
00:26:24,291 --> 00:26:28,086
it flows steadily
and eventually reaches the sea.

247
00:26:28,712 --> 00:26:33,299
I hope Tae-ha will live his life
so that he can one day go down the path

248
00:26:33,300 --> 00:26:35,468
he wants to go.

249
00:26:38,305 --> 00:26:39,221
Why not?

250
00:26:39,222 --> 00:26:41,974
Whatever our Tae-ha does,
it'll be good no matter what.

251
00:26:41,975 --> 00:26:44,810
<i>Even when you were a baby,</i>

252
00:26:44,811 --> 00:26:49,024
you were always so sure
of what you wanted to do.

253
00:26:49,899 --> 00:26:52,694
But you didn't get to live it out
because of me.

254
00:26:55,030 --> 00:26:57,449
When I meet your mom in the afterlife,

255
00:26:58,366 --> 00:27:00,702
I won't be able to face her.

256
00:27:01,411 --> 00:27:02,328
Grandma.

257
00:27:02,329 --> 00:27:07,417
So, can you do me a favor
and help me save face?

258
00:27:12,213 --> 00:27:14,549
Be happy, Tae-ha.

259
00:27:21,097 --> 00:27:22,849
From now on,

260
00:27:23,350 --> 00:27:26,018
don't let anyone interfere with your life.

261
00:27:26,019 --> 00:27:30,815
Just think about yourself and be happy.

262
00:27:32,942 --> 00:27:37,613
You've already been through
so many rough valleys,

263
00:27:37,614 --> 00:27:39,199
so from now on,

264
00:27:40,075 --> 00:27:41,785
go find your ocean.

265
00:27:42,661 --> 00:27:45,622
Go find your happiness, okay?

266
00:27:53,004 --> 00:27:53,838
That's my boy.

267
00:27:59,052 --> 00:28:00,387
Oh my…

268
00:28:12,941 --> 00:28:14,651
Oh, my baby.

269
00:28:17,529 --> 00:28:21,741
THE LATE JANG HYE-SU

270
00:28:25,328 --> 00:28:28,456
Hello, ma'am. My name is Go Eun-sae.

271
00:28:37,674 --> 00:28:38,925
Won't you introduce me?

272
00:28:45,181 --> 00:28:46,725
She's the woman I like.

273
00:28:56,776 --> 00:28:57,610
That's it?

274
00:29:00,363 --> 00:29:02,574
My mom knows everything,
even if I don't tell her.

275
00:29:18,381 --> 00:29:21,049
Did you really not have
anything else to say?

276
00:29:21,050 --> 00:29:23,762
"She's the woman I like"? That's it?

277
00:29:24,262 --> 00:29:25,597
Do I need to say more?

278
00:29:26,139 --> 00:29:28,140
You have so much to say about me.

279
00:29:28,141 --> 00:29:31,977
Like how I'm so pretty, I wouldn't look
out of place walking a red carpet.

280
00:29:31,978 --> 00:29:35,773
Or how I'm so talented that I became
a star prosecutor at a young age.

281
00:29:35,774 --> 00:29:40,527
Or how I'm the woman
you'd give your life for.

282
00:29:40,528 --> 00:29:43,323
Or how I'm the woman
you want to meet again in your next life.

283
00:29:44,115 --> 00:29:47,534
You're not cool at all. So uncool.

284
00:29:47,535 --> 00:29:49,370
Right, Blessing?

285
00:29:52,999 --> 00:29:54,125
What's this?

286
00:30:19,901 --> 00:30:22,070
Everyone says they want me to be happy.

287
00:30:26,407 --> 00:30:27,408
Now…

288
00:30:29,494 --> 00:30:30,745
I want to be happy too.

289
00:30:41,381 --> 00:30:42,590
But…

290
00:30:44,384 --> 00:30:45,969
my happiness is Go Eun-sae.

291
00:30:50,139 --> 00:30:51,850
I know I'm uncool,

292
00:30:53,476 --> 00:30:55,103
but I don't know what else to say.

293
00:30:59,607 --> 00:31:01,693
I have to be with you to be happy.

294
00:31:14,998 --> 00:31:15,832
Will you…

295
00:31:18,209 --> 00:31:19,210
marry me?

296
00:31:31,931 --> 00:31:33,808
I think I already answered.

297
00:31:37,145 --> 00:31:39,606
I said that even though
I got my memory back,

298
00:31:40,231 --> 00:31:42,692
I still like Jang Tae-ha.

299
00:31:59,876 --> 00:32:03,004
Who else would I marry if not Jang Tae-ha?

300
00:32:18,394 --> 00:32:19,520
I love you.

301
00:32:20,730 --> 00:32:21,731
I love you too.

302
00:32:40,249 --> 00:32:42,292
- So cute!
- Adorable!

303
00:32:42,293 --> 00:32:43,418
How sweet.

304
00:32:43,419 --> 00:32:45,046
Would you look at that!

305
00:32:46,547 --> 00:32:49,509
I told you,
that dog is better than people.

306
00:33:12,073 --> 00:33:13,116
How pretty.

307
00:33:19,580 --> 00:33:23,668
With this, these two have pledged
to be one forever.

308
00:33:30,466 --> 00:33:31,550
Next,

309
00:33:31,551 --> 00:33:36,054
we have a song to celebrate
the marriage of the bride and groom.

310
00:33:36,055 --> 00:33:39,683
Please welcome them
with a big round of applause.

311
00:33:39,684 --> 00:33:41,309
The fairies of our village.

312
00:33:41,310 --> 00:33:44,063
A song
from Taffy Village's very own S.E.S!

313
00:34:14,218 --> 00:34:15,595
What's he doing?

314
00:34:21,809 --> 00:34:22,852
That's it!

315
00:34:24,395 --> 00:34:28,065
<i>Why won't you tell me
Things that have already passed</i>

316
00:34:28,066 --> 00:34:29,441
You look great!

317
00:34:29,442 --> 00:34:31,319
<i>A cliché-filled old love story</i>

318
00:34:33,863 --> 00:34:36,198
<i>Tell me honestly</i>

319
00:34:36,199 --> 00:34:42,080
<i>But to me, you're the only one</i>

320
00:34:43,247 --> 00:34:45,373
<i>Don't be afraid</i>

321
00:34:45,374 --> 00:34:47,959
<i>I'm by your side</i>

322
00:34:47,960 --> 00:34:52,172
<i>To the end of our lives</i>

323
00:34:52,173 --> 00:34:55,717
<i>I hope you trust me</i>

324
00:34:55,718 --> 00:34:57,804
<i>Stay with me</i>

325
00:35:01,140 --> 00:35:05,477
<i>I'm becoming more like you</i>

326
00:35:05,478 --> 00:35:07,605
<i>Watch over me</i>

327
00:35:14,529 --> 00:35:16,239
Bride, you can throw the bouquet now.

328
00:35:18,241 --> 00:35:20,034
One, two, three!

329
00:35:27,375 --> 00:35:28,625
What the…

330
00:35:28,626 --> 00:35:29,835
- Oh my.
- What happened?

331
00:35:29,836 --> 00:35:30,877
What should we do?

332
00:35:30,878 --> 00:35:32,255
- Throw it again.
- Here.

333
00:35:34,257 --> 00:35:35,507
- It's Su-ji!
- Yeah.

334
00:35:35,508 --> 00:35:36,843
No takebacks now.

335
00:35:39,554 --> 00:35:40,930
What's he doing?

336
00:35:41,973 --> 00:35:44,225
- Here.
- What's with him?

337
00:35:44,851 --> 00:35:46,811
He gave her flowers.

338
00:35:48,563 --> 00:35:50,481
What's going on with those two?

339
00:35:53,484 --> 00:35:55,987
- Love is in the air!
- Did he just cut those flowers?

340
00:35:56,571 --> 00:35:57,737
Get married!

341
00:35:57,738 --> 00:35:59,031
Accept his love!

342
00:36:00,908 --> 00:36:03,202
- What the…
- What?

343
00:36:09,167 --> 00:36:11,001
It's raining!

344
00:36:11,002 --> 00:36:13,087
Where do we go? Where?

345
00:36:13,588 --> 00:36:16,507
It's a sun-shower! Maybe a tiger
is getting married today too!

346
00:36:17,466 --> 00:36:18,800
- Right?
- Come here!

347
00:36:18,801 --> 00:36:21,386
Tae-ha, Eun-sae, come here. Hurry!

348
00:36:21,387 --> 00:36:22,512
Come on!

349
00:36:22,513 --> 00:36:24,682
- You're getting wet!
- Get in here!

350
00:36:25,892 --> 00:36:28,269
Man, what will we do?

351
00:36:29,312 --> 00:36:30,313
Goodness.

352
00:36:41,032 --> 00:36:44,702
<i>For whatever reason, it always rained
on the hardest days of my life.</i>

353
00:36:46,120 --> 00:36:47,914
<i>In my bleakest moments,</i>

354
00:36:48,414 --> 00:36:52,126
<i>there was nothing
to shield me from the rain.</i>

355
00:36:52,627 --> 00:36:54,921
<i>It felt like a reminder
of how hopeless things were.</i>

356
00:36:55,421 --> 00:36:56,589
<i>So I don't like rain.</i>

357
00:36:58,633 --> 00:37:00,384
<i>Let's weather it together from now on.</i>

358
00:37:02,220 --> 00:37:04,222
I'll be with you.

359
00:37:24,033 --> 00:37:26,409
- What are they doing?
- Why are they out in the rain?

360
00:37:26,410 --> 00:37:28,203
Come over here!

361
00:37:28,204 --> 00:37:30,580
I guess this will be another memory.

362
00:37:30,581 --> 00:37:32,208
Let's just play in the rain!

363
00:37:43,135 --> 00:37:44,094
Let's join them.

364
00:37:44,095 --> 00:37:46,264
Screw it. Let's go!

365
00:39:56,310 --> 00:39:59,771
We can't go on a honeymoon
because there are so many trials lined up,

366
00:39:59,772 --> 00:40:02,983
but we should at least
make it feel like our wedding night.

367
00:40:03,484 --> 00:40:04,318
Ta-da!

368
00:40:04,902 --> 00:40:07,696
They say it's a miracle remedy
that makes you young and firm.

369
00:40:08,197 --> 00:40:11,866
This is lion's mane liquor.

370
00:40:11,867 --> 00:40:13,494
It's super precious.

371
00:40:16,455 --> 00:40:17,748
This…

372
00:40:18,290 --> 00:40:20,418
How long has this been here?

373
00:40:20,918 --> 00:40:22,460
- It's a secret.
- A secret?

374
00:40:22,461 --> 00:40:23,504
Cheers!

375
00:40:34,390 --> 00:40:37,810
Shall we go do what we need to do now?

376
00:40:39,186 --> 00:40:40,020
Yeah.

377
00:40:44,108 --> 00:40:45,151
Let's go.

378
00:40:46,986 --> 00:40:47,862
Go Eun…

379
00:40:51,657 --> 00:40:52,491
shway.

380
00:40:59,081 --> 00:41:02,417
I re… really…

381
00:41:02,418 --> 00:41:03,294
Yeah?

382
00:41:08,007 --> 00:41:09,216
I really

383
00:41:09,717 --> 00:41:10,634
like

384
00:41:11,594 --> 00:41:12,636
Go Eun-sae.

385
00:41:15,431 --> 00:41:19,434
She said it was meant to make you younger,
but how much younger did you get?

386
00:41:19,435 --> 00:41:20,852
- Babe.
- Yeah?

387
00:41:20,853 --> 00:41:23,647
What am I supposed to do with a baby?

388
00:41:24,648 --> 00:41:25,774
I'm happy.

389
00:41:26,567 --> 00:41:27,443
So happy.

390
00:41:32,781 --> 00:41:34,532
- Babe?
- Yeah?

391
00:41:34,533 --> 00:41:36,242
Now's not the time to pass out.

392
00:41:36,243 --> 00:41:38,495
Get up. Babe.

393
00:41:38,496 --> 00:41:39,538
<i>Oppa.</i>

394
00:41:41,415 --> 00:41:45,461
- Yeah?
- <i>Oppa</i>.

395
00:41:49,465 --> 00:41:50,549
Jang Tae-ha.

396
00:41:53,511 --> 00:41:54,929
Mr. Jang Tae-ha!

397
00:41:55,429 --> 00:41:56,972
I'm so happy.

398
00:42:09,860 --> 00:42:10,778
Water…

399
00:42:11,278 --> 00:42:12,196
Water.

400
00:42:24,083 --> 00:42:25,084
Did you…

401
00:42:26,669 --> 00:42:27,628
Did you sleep well?

402
00:42:30,089 --> 00:42:33,508
What do you think?
When you let our one and only first night

403
00:42:33,509 --> 00:42:34,885
go to waste like that?

404
00:42:35,386 --> 00:42:38,221
How come I've never seen you
get drunk until now,

405
00:42:38,222 --> 00:42:41,600
and you pass out on our first night?
On our important wedding night?

406
00:42:47,439 --> 00:42:49,441
Does it… have to be at night?

407
00:42:52,027 --> 00:42:52,987
Can't it be

408
00:42:53,654 --> 00:42:56,240
our first morning too?

409
00:43:02,371 --> 00:43:06,041
Babe! What are you doing?

410
00:43:07,835 --> 00:43:09,878
<i>Everyone's life has a genre.</i>

411
00:43:10,379 --> 00:43:13,716
Ms. Min Su-ji and I are planning
to get married.

412
00:43:25,769 --> 00:43:27,354
<i>At times, romance.</i>

413
00:43:31,483 --> 00:43:33,444
- Dig deeper.
- You got it.

414
00:43:34,737 --> 00:43:36,113
<i>At times, film noir.</i>

415
00:43:38,282 --> 00:43:41,576
If we don't bury it deep,
the kimchi won't taste good. So dig deep.

416
00:43:41,577 --> 00:43:42,494
Yes.

417
00:43:42,995 --> 00:43:43,829
My back.

418
00:43:52,296 --> 00:43:54,214
Are you okay, sir?

419
00:43:56,425 --> 00:43:58,384
You absolute piece of filth!

420
00:43:58,385 --> 00:44:00,678
- No, Jeong-hwa. I'm okay.
- Look at this bastard!

421
00:44:00,679 --> 00:44:02,138
I'm okay.

422
00:44:02,139 --> 00:44:03,264
Hey, you bastard!

423
00:44:03,265 --> 00:44:04,474
I said I'm okay!

424
00:44:04,475 --> 00:44:05,516
I'm sorry!

425
00:44:05,517 --> 00:44:07,144
Dig deep! Deeper!

426
00:44:12,483 --> 00:44:14,151
<i>At times, horror.</i>

427
00:44:18,822 --> 00:44:21,240
You don't have a middle ground, do you?

428
00:44:21,241 --> 00:44:22,743
RANK: 82/82

429
00:44:29,291 --> 00:44:30,417
I hear it.

430
00:44:31,126 --> 00:44:32,251
I can hear it.

431
00:44:32,252 --> 00:44:34,921
I can hear the revered spirit.

432
00:44:34,922 --> 00:44:36,173
What?

433
00:44:45,474 --> 00:44:48,310
The revered spirit has returned!

434
00:44:49,478 --> 00:44:50,312
The heck?

435
00:44:51,480 --> 00:44:53,273
Revered spirit!

436
00:44:54,274 --> 00:44:56,693
Revered spirit, you have returned!

437
00:44:56,694 --> 00:44:58,695
You don't know how long I've waited!

438
00:44:58,696 --> 00:45:01,073
<i>And at times, fantasy.</i>

439
00:45:16,255 --> 00:45:17,755
Adding more photos again?

440
00:45:17,756 --> 00:45:20,634
Yeah, we should
stay on top of organizing them.

441
00:45:21,343 --> 00:45:23,095
You really love taking photos.

442
00:45:23,679 --> 00:45:25,930
After losing my memory,

443
00:45:25,931 --> 00:45:28,225
I realized that these are like
emergency funds.

444
00:45:29,810 --> 00:45:33,021
When I'm having a hard time,
when I'm exhausted,

445
00:45:33,522 --> 00:45:34,982
when I don't know where to go…

446
00:45:35,858 --> 00:45:39,611
These are like emergency funds
you can dip into during tough times.

447
00:45:43,323 --> 00:45:45,867
<i>Though the genre may change unpredictably,</i>

448
00:45:45,868 --> 00:45:49,538
<i>you share every scene with people
who stand by your side.</i>

449
00:45:50,247 --> 00:45:53,208
<i>And the memories you make with them
come together, frame by frame,</i>

450
00:45:53,792 --> 00:45:56,170
<i>to complete the drama we call life.</i>

451
00:45:58,213 --> 00:46:03,010
<i>Perhaps living is all about remembering
the scenes that have passed.</i>

452
00:46:09,308 --> 00:46:10,934
Say hello. They're from this village.

453
00:46:14,229 --> 00:46:15,063
Stop right there.

454
00:46:16,023 --> 00:46:17,191
Eun-sae's here.

455
00:46:22,029 --> 00:46:23,780
<i>Happy birthday to you…</i>

456
00:46:23,781 --> 00:46:26,574
<i>If I leave something like this behind,</i>

457
00:46:26,575 --> 00:46:29,661
<i>even if I happen to lose my memory again,</i>

458
00:46:30,162 --> 00:46:33,206
I think I'd be able to believe

459
00:46:33,207 --> 00:46:36,835
that I lived a happy life
with my loved ones.

460
00:46:41,507 --> 00:46:42,841
No need to worry.

461
00:46:43,342 --> 00:46:45,302
I can just tell you everything.

462
00:46:47,471 --> 00:46:48,639
You're right.

463
00:46:50,098 --> 00:46:53,143
Now I have someone who will remember
every moment of my life.

464
00:47:00,442 --> 00:47:01,943
<i>You must like taking pictures.</i>

465
00:47:01,944 --> 00:47:03,904
I've been taking pictures
since I was a kid.

466
00:47:04,404 --> 00:47:08,282
If I had a mom and dad, they would have
taken pictures of me growing up.

467
00:47:08,283 --> 00:47:11,286
They would have remembered
and told me about it later.

468
00:47:12,204 --> 00:47:16,208
Someone like me can't reminisce about
the past unless I leave something behind.

469
00:47:17,751 --> 00:47:21,338
So this is what it feels like
to have family.

470
00:47:36,937 --> 00:47:38,814
Should we capture this moment too?

471
00:47:40,691 --> 00:47:41,650
Should we?

472
00:47:44,111 --> 00:47:45,737
Three, two…

473
00:47:46,238 --> 00:47:48,322
- Wait.
- Blessing, you want in too?

474
00:47:48,323 --> 00:47:50,742
Look at the camera. Three, two, one.

475
00:47:56,540 --> 00:47:57,833
It came out great.

476
00:48:01,712 --> 00:48:03,255
- It's pretty.
- Yeah.

477
00:48:15,976 --> 00:48:18,603
- I should put this in the album too.
- Right now?

478
00:48:18,604 --> 00:48:19,563
A little later.

479
00:49:48,318 --> 00:49:52,614
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
